* `stdin`: Set to `false` because we don't need to read from stdin.
* `ws`: Set to `true` to allow websockets to work correctly.

With these options set, the proxy will forward all incoming requests to the `target` URL without modifying the headers. It will also forward all incoming headers and responses back to the client without modifying them.

Note that this proxy will not add any custom headers or modify the headers in any way. It will only act as a middleware, forwarding requests and responses as is.

You can test this proxy by making a request to `http://localhost:8080` and verifying that the response is the same as if you had made the request directly to the target URL. You can also use a tool like `curl` to test the proxy:
